{"fetchedAt":"2026-09-28T12:56:25.816Z","overview":{"Symbol":"PHIN","Name":"PHINIA Inc.","Description":"PHINIA Inc. engages in the development, design, and manufacture of integrated components and systems. The company operates through Fuel Systems and Aftermarket segments. The Fuel Systems segment provides advanced fuel injection systems, including pumps, injectors, fuel rail assemblies, and engine control modules; fuel delivery modules; canisters; sensors; and electronic control modules. This segment also offers complete systems comprising software and calibration services that reduce emissions and enhance fuel economy for traditional and hybrid applications. The Aftermarket segment engages in the provision of maintenance, test equipment, and vehicle diagnostics solutions; original equipment service solutions and remanufactured products; and sale of sale of starters and alternators to original equipment manufacturers. Its products are used for commercial vehicles and industrial applications, such as medium-duty and heavy-duty trucks, buses and other off-highway construction, marine, agricultural and aerospace and defense applications; light commercial vehicles comprising vans and trucks; and light passenger vehicles, including passenger cars, mini-vans, cross-overs and sport-utility vehicles. PHINIA Inc. was incorporated in 2023 and is based in Auburn Hills, Michigan.","CIK":"","Exchange":"NYSE","Currency":"USD","Country":"United States","Sector":"Consumer Cyclical","Industry":"Auto Parts","Address":"3000 University Drive, Auburn Hills, MI, 48326, United States","FiscalYearEnd":"","LatestQuarter":"","MarketCapitalization":"2273027072","EBITDA":"486000000","PERatio":"17.776505","PEGRatio":"","BookValue":"42.06","DividendPerShare":"1.2","DividendYield":"0.019299999","EPS":"3.49","RevenuePerShareTTM":"95.257","ProfitMargin":"0.03734","OperatingMarginTTM":"0.077659994","ReturnOnAssetsTTM":"0.05235","ReturnOnEquityTTM":"0.08523","RevenueTTM":"3615000064","GrossProfitTTM